{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling on 599cadaa: head F's pin list, and no live activation.\n\n1. The three named pins change, as you list them: the maintained\n   Grow Room for its own spelling, base Change for its own spelling,\n   and the maintained Grow Site because it embeds the Room digest.\n\n2. The eight derived identities change too. After F, every\n   definition that current source generates is in canonical\n   spelling: the six Change descendants, the demo Room and the demo\n   Site. One generator line stays. A generator that still emitted\n   the redundant spelling would fail the rule of request item 1 and\n   the test of item 3. This amends 2ad35350: eleven identities\n   change, not two.\n\n3. Recorded history does not change. The signed demo package, the\n   archive histories and the simulator histories keep Room b89e7f84\n   and Site d2bc830e and their bytes. Do not regenerate or re-sign\n   them. Tests read them as recorded inputs.\n\n4. No live activation. The new pins take effect only in rooms\n   created after F. The identifiers cutover (c0a795e7) retires and\n   recreates the Grow, Lending and Site rooms, and the planner signs\n   the new release then. I withdraw the live part of request item 2:\n   F writes no migration plan for live rooms, no activation act and\n   no rollback. The PD-2 note says this in two sentences.\n\n5. Rooms created before F keep working after F deploys, until the\n   cutover. This binds your choice between refusing and normalizing\n   in request item 1:\n   - A journal recorded before F replays and verifies after F, with\n     its definition digests unchanged.\n   - The digest of a definition that is already canonical does not\n     change. The Lending, Counter and platform pins stay byte-equal.\n   - A deployed Worker still serves a room that pins the old Room,\n     Site or Change bytes.\n   The note states, with file and line, how a Worker finds a room's\n   pinned Room, Site and Change definition. It names the existing\n   case that replays a recorded old-spelling history under the new\n   code. If no such case exists, add one over a history that the\n   repository already holds. If any path finds a definition through\n   current source by digest, keep the old bytes for that path as\n   recorded data and say so. The cutover removes them.\n\n6. The test of item 3 covers every pinned definition and every\n   generated identity. It excludes the recorded histories of point 3\n   by an exact list, each row with its reason.\n\n7. The demo clone's receiver stays tied to the maintained Room, and\n   follows that Room's new digest. Make no semantic repair in F. If\n   you judge the difference a defect, file it to the planner as a\n   finding with the two lines of source.\n\n8. The Scale workflow step of 0b92c593 stands. F does not extend\n   `scripts/check-definition-pins.mjs` beyond Lending and Counter.\n   Head G does that with its exact witnesses.\n\nThe kernel filing rule of docs/kernel.md section 7 applies to the\nvalidator change, as the request says. I deploy after the landing\nand check that the live Grow rooms still answer.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}